--- body ---
## Context

Child of tickets/1004, blocked by 1005. All coaching numbers are derived
at read time (spec §6); nothing judged is ever stored in the records.

## Actions

1. One query tool over a project's attribution records producing the
   three surfaces: per-seat scores (labeled-game catch rate, noise rate,
   run-failure rate, Beta-Binomial credible intervals), reviewer-reviewer
   pairwise concordance tables (conditioned on defect-bearing games),
   stratified by writer (writer-reviewer concordance is incomputable —
   the writer is a stratification variable, spec §4.3, §6), and marginal
   unique-catch coverage of seat B given seat A. The 0937 box-3 hand-off
   (log 2026-10-02T10:24Z) is subsumed here: the run-failure rate derives
   from the required `status:` field (spec §4.6) and the query output is
   the non-human channel; a machine-readable flag for recently-failed
   seats is an open question for the author, not assumed by this ticket.
2. Migrate skills/roar/enumerate-merges.py here (per the celebration
   teardown, spec §9): enumerate merged PRs since a reference is exactly
   the enumeration the query needs; the write path is deleted in 1009,
   the read capability survives here.
3. Malformed record lines WARN on stderr, never silently dropped (the
   harvest convention).
4. Act-on thresholds follow spec §7: report always, act only when
   intervals justify it.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Scores table renders from real records with credible intervals
- [x] Correlation table renders with the four concordance cells per pair
- [x] Marginal coverage column distinguishes a duplicate seat from a
      complementary one on the same records

## Raid annotation (2026-10-03, imagine pass)
PREMISE: Holds, with one ticket-vs-spec contradiction (fixed — log 2026-10-03) and one hand-off made explicit. Zero attribution records exist yet (correct: 1005 unmerged; the gate is real). `skills/roar/scores` does not exist — the drifted scorecard parser is the `scores` subcommand in `skills/reviewers/reviewers.sh:821-895` (greps trial cards out of erg logs; 21/31 recent scorecards use rejected prose variants, spec §1.2); it dies in 1009 — 1007 builds a replacement over the record format, not a port of that bash parser. `enumerate-merges.py` exists exactly as §9 describes.
REIMAGINE: One Python query tool in `scripts/` (spec §3 puts the enumerate-merges utility and shared substrate in `scripts/`; `skills/roar/` is the hot write path and step 2 dies in 1009). Input: project repo root (default cwd); reads `memory/journal/**/*-review-attribution-prNNNN.md`. Three surfaces: (1) Scores — per seat and per recorded model version (§7: a model change splits history): catch/noise/run-failure rates, each Beta-Binomial with Jeffreys prior Beta(1/2,1/2), 90% CrI; no scipy in `requirements-dev.txt` and `tests/test_deps_declared.py` derives imports from source, so a pure-Python regularized incomplete beta (continued fraction + bisection, ~40 lines) — a normal/Wilson approximation would violate the pre-registered §7. (2) Correlation — reviewer-reviewer four-cell concordance (both/unique-A/unique-B/neither) conditioned on defect-bearing games only (§1.1 base-rate discipline), plus Jaccard catch-overlap and shared-hallucination rate; the writer stratifies, never enters as a pair member (§4.3). (3) Marginal coverage — unique-catch rate of B given A over games where both ran. Join key: anchored path:line; a catch = `adopted: yes` finding or defect-confirmed event matching the seat's anchor (§6). `enumerate-merges.py` migration: move to `scripts/` in this PR and update the three references in the same PR — the step-2 call in `skills/roar/SKILL.md:89`, `tests/test_roar_enumerate_merges.py` (ENUMERATE constant), `tests/test_roar_step2_attribution.py:185` (hard-coded string) — or the tree is broken between 1007 and 1009. The migrated enumeration also serves §9's backfill join (reviewed merges with no record → §4.8 fail-loud). Malformed lines: the harvest convention already in tree (`reviewers.sh:852/877` WARN-and-continue; the octopus skip) — WARN the offending line to stderr, skip it, never a silent drop or hard abort.
ANTIPATTERNS: No storing derived judgments in records (§2/§6: derived, never stored). No prose parsing (rule 1; the 0348 scorecard-poisoning lesson). No silent drops. No writer-reviewer concordance (§4.3: incomputable — the ticket's original wording, now fixed). No acting on correlation without interval justification (§7: report always, act only when intervals justify; eliminate/promote thresholds printed as labels, not enforced). No premature multi-project or cross-model-version aggregation (§4.7, §7). No normal-approximation CrIs; no conditioning concordance on all games; no recovering tickets from branch names (close-commit scan only).
EXIT-CRITERIA: Box 1 — a table rendered over live journal records after 1005 lands (the harness journal is already v8; the first real reviewed merge yields the first record); tmp-journal fixtures are unit evidence only. Box 2 — records with ≥2 seats, shared and unique anchors, ≥1 defect label (unlabeled games are excluded — fixtures must include `adopted: yes` or a defect-confirmed line); four cells per pair, writer stratification column, WARN convention exercised on a deliberately malformed line. Box 3 — fixtures need both a near-total-overlap (duplicate) and a near-disjoint (complementary) seat pair on the same records so the distinction is falsifiable (anti-tautology guard). Verdict: reword (applied — spec §4.3 contradiction fixed; 0937 box-3 subsumption made explicit).

## Raid Imagine refresh (2026-10-05, next attribution batch)
PREMISE: PASS. Real1190 wrap-up records1185/1186 now exist and parse (10/12 attempts,3 adopted anchors each). Use shared reader and explicitly declared bounded SciPy betaincinv; official inverse-beta primitive replaces prior custom-CDF suggestion while fixed Jeffreys prior and central90% interval remain unchanged. Record precise game/anchor/attempt denominators and honest unconfirmed/shared-unconfirmed proxies; exact identities and writer strata preserve provenance. Minimal PR/merge metadata added to migrated enumeration for missing-record coverage.
BLIND-SPOT: Multiple valid dated records for one PR are ambiguous. WARN and exclude all duplicate-PR records; no double counting, latest selection or implicit consolidation. Filename/date uniqueness is not game uniqueness.
DRIFT GUARD: Three criteria unchanged, statistics policy untouched. New dependency/denominator disclosure is implementation choice; no automatic roster actions or machine-failed-seat flag introduced.

## Raid Plan refresh (2026-10-05, next attribution batch)

Decision: one read-only project query, existing strict fixed-line reader, ordinary counters/sets and declared SciPy special.betaincinv for fixed Jeffreys intervals. This replaces prior no-scipy implementation suggestion, not statistics policy: Beta(s+.5,n-s+.5), central .05/.95 quantiles, always report, no automatic roster action. Declare bounded compatible scipy in requirements-dev.txt; actual ambient import exists but declaration is required by tests/test_deps_declared.py. Official API https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.special.betaincinv.html . Do not implement custom CDF. Root is to approve this bounded dependency tradeoff before implementation.

Actions:
1. First meaningful test: hand-authored multi-game record dataset whose duplicate pair has zero unique-B and complementary pair has positive unique-B; include postmerge-only defect, third-seat labels, clean game excluded, failed/skipped attempts, writer/version split. Invoke actual query CLI and assert exact denominators/four cells/status counts, not just rendered headings.
2. scripts/attribution_query.py imports parse_record. Read only current project's memory journal attribution-kind filenames; malformed input warns filename + parser line error and counts skipped whole records; encrypted input counted unavailable, no decryption/plaintext fallback. Do not count invalid partial record or fabricate missing journals. Expose structured JSON and readable table from same derived result; no persist/cache/roster edits.
3. Define and document identity exact seat/runtime/model/model-version; writer exact runtime/model/version/effort strata, never pair member. For each PR/identity, union findings for binary game catch (at least one anchor in global confirmed labels); no duplicated game credit from repeated attempts. Retain raw ran/failed/skipped attempt counts separately and disclose run-failure denominator failed/(ran+failed), skipped separate. Catch denominator labeled games with identity ran. Pair comparisons only both-ran labeled PRs, four binary-any-catch cells; Jaccard from confirmed anchor sets separately, not ambiguous game cell inflation. Unique-B coverage is label anchors B caught and A did not, with explicit labeled both-ran game success denominator; disclose same-game different anchors so both-catch can still include complementary coverage. No stripping round names or pooled versions.
4. Noise score explicitly nonconfirmed-finding share proxy among emitted findings, after applying later event labels; identical finding anchors across attempts do not silently become extra game trials. Shared hallucination is shared nonconfirmed-anchor proxy, label honesty in output. Print successes/trials and prior-only no-data intervals, raw attempted/ran/failed/skipped counts. Keep literal fixed §7 elimination/promote guidance; no changing upper-bound comparison because counterintuitive. Live mismatched selection isn't same frozen board: no automatic promotion verdict.
5. git mv skills/roar/enumerate-merges.py → scripts/enumerate-merges.py retaining legacy fields/behavior. Add minimal PR number + merge SHA/date for read coverage, sourced from actual merge subject/commit, no branch digit guessing. Update Roar same-shell root command and tests/test_roar_enumerate_merges.py plus tests/test_roar_step2_attribution.py exact snippet replacement. Preserve until, first-parent, octopus WARN and close-commit ticket logic. New metadata must not break legacy celebration writer compatibility, inspected/tested before1009 deletes it.
6. Enumerate explicitly requested git range (no hidden new sentinel), report PRs lacking attribution as missing evidence rather than infer reviewers. Validate genuine journal record(s) produced by authorized live wrap-up, show command/count/output. Synthetic design template cannot satisfy real-record criterion. No use pending private metadata without clearance.

Dependencies: merged1005;1006 events optional input and parser already accepts them. No1009 dependency. Path inventory: newquery, newquerytests, requirements-dev.txt, scripts/enumerate-merges.py + removedoldpath, Roar, existingtwoenumtestfiles, approvedspecimplementationnote, own1007ticket/archive = 10 content paths, 12 diff entries, below15 after annotationprelude base. If more docs/framework needed split rather than exceed guard. Skill frontmatter unchanged, run catalog drift.

Numerical meaningful checks: independent hand-pinned oracle constants; Beta(.5,.5) analytic arcsine endpoint; symmetry for s vs n-s; extreme zero/all counts and large n. These test betaincinv argument/prior/tail mistakes independently rather than compare function to itself. Dataset exact expected game counts catches anchor/game conflation, clean-game dilution, treating failed seat as miss, duplicate attempts, version pooling, hidden writer pairing and false-noise after event confirmation. CLI malformed/encrypted/no-record diagnostics. Real enumerator migration and end-to-end bash invocation regressions remain green. Full check once after targeted tests, genuine journal acceptance observed honestly.

Risks needing explicit acceptance: ratio/proxy names and per-game vs anchor definitions were under-specified; implementation note must disclose them without pretending proven hallucinations or changing fixed thresholds. Live round-qualified identities may initially yield sparse pair data; report it rather than normalize names. Cross-review attempts can have different coordinate provenance; query uses literal contract join, not fuzzy semantic defect clustering.

Plan supplement: duplicate PR records are ambiguous; WARN and exclude all duplicates from query, backfill and coverage until separately resolved. No implicit snapshot consolidation.

